# Day 1 — Data Cleaning & Preparation

### What I learned
- Basic principles of data cleaning
- The importance of correct formatting before analysis
- How to work with Google Sheets efficiently

---

### What I did (Step by step)
- Made a copy of the dataset and set language to Ukrainian
- Renamed sheets to “Платежі” and “MCC”
- Locked (froze) the first row and made the header bold
- Adjusted column width to display all content
- Removed unnecessary hyphens in columns F and G (Find & Replace)
- Deleted incorrect rows with inconsistent data
- Applied number formatting (2 decimals) for columns D and F

---

### Tools & skills used
- Formatting (bold, freeze row, adjust width)
- Find & Replace
- Correct data types
- Basic cleaning rules

---

### Notes
This day was focused on preparing the dataset for further analysis.  
All transformations make data clean and structured, which helps avoid mistakes in next steps.
